        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    cost_of_equity = 0.08\n    after_tax_cost_of_debt = 0.04\n    equity_market_value = 2_000_000\n    debt_market_value = 1_000_000\n    corporate_tax_rate = 0.25\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    total_market_value = equity_market_value + debt_market_value\n    equity_weight = equity_market_value / total_market_value\n    debt_weight = debt_market_value / total_market_value\n\n    # The stated 4% debt cost is already after tax, so the tax rate is not applied again.\n    wacc = (\n        equity_weight * cost_of_equity\n        + debt_weight * after_tax_cost_of_debt\n    )\n    answer = round(wacc * 100, 2)\n\n    # return answer\n    return answer\n```",
